   ]
  },
  "scope_notes": "The PR contains a small 20-line logic fix in src/node/txorphanage.cpp along with a large (~570-line) new fuzz harness in src/test/fuzz/p2p_1p1c_liveness.cpp.",
  "changed_since_previous": "Rebased and marked as the base for follow-up PR #36506.",
  "card": "This pull request fixes a transaction relay liveness hole in TxOrphanage where an orphan queued for reconsideration is abandoned if its assigned announcer disconnects or is evicted before retry. Because the transaction remains held in the orphanage, subsequent announcements from honest peers are ignored, allowing peers to deliberately delay transactions such as CPFP children until eviction. TxOrphanage now reassigns reconsideration to a remaining announcer on erasure. The PR also introduces an end-to-end fuzz harness that reproduces this vulnerability on master in under an hour and validates parent-child relay under adversarial conditions, unblocking follow-up hole fixes in #36506.",
